# gr-L1-dependency-graph-quality-gate — LLM-Driven Colang Implementation
# Layer: L1 — fires at L1-planning-dependency-mapper-evaluator's post_execution
# Validates L1-planning-dependency-mapper's RESULTANT output (not the evaluator's own bookkeeping)
# Python actions preserved in actions.py for reference/hybrid mode
#
# NOTE: in this LLM-only mode, the "independent" DFS cycle check and
# longest-path computation are performed BY THE LLM itself, per prompts.yml's
# step-by-step instructions — this mode is weaker than the Python-hybrid
# mode (dependency_graph_quality_gate.co) for this particular guardrail,
# since a graph traversal is exactly the kind of deterministic computation
# an LLM can get wrong. Prefer the Python-hybrid mode in production.

define flow check output dependency graph quality gate
  """LLM independently re-derives cycle_check and critical_path from the resultant output and validates against L1-planning-dependency-mapper's own schema and evaluation.md rubric."""
  $result = execute self_check_output

  if not $result
    bot block dependency graph quality gate violation
    stop

define bot block dependency graph quality gate violation
  "L1-planning-dependency-mapper's resultant output (post-evaluation) failed its quality gate: a schema violation, a dangling edge, an independently re-derived cycle_check or critical_path that disagrees with what the resultant content claims, a cyclic graph not escalated to status failed, or an FR coverage mismatch. The workflow cannot proceed to backlog-prioritizer/design-hld with an unverified dependency graph. Retrying."
